KZ3 patch 2062 (RSX pass 62): window size apart from the guest's 1280x720 output.
rsx_window_size.h (new, platform-free): KZ3_WINDOW_SIZE parsing (WxH, 720p/900p/1080p/1440p/2160p/4k), the largest
aspect-correct client inside a size, the WM_SIZING correction, and (Win32) rsx_win_client_size + rsx_win_size_msg
used by both window owners: rsx_null_backend.c (the window KZ3 runs in; the live-draw swap chain binds to it) and
rsx_d3d12_backend.c. The window's client size comes from KZ3_WINDOW_SIZE (default: the guest size, as before), keeps the guest aspect (a 16:10 request becomes the
largest 16:9 inside it) and shrinks it to the monitor's work area; WM_SIZING keeps the aspect while dragging,
WM_GETMINMAXINFO makes maximize the largest aspect-correct client, centred, minimum 320x180. The swap chain stays at
the guest size and DXGI_SCALING_STRETCH (its default) scales it to the client area at present, so nothing in the
renderer changes. Log: [window]. Host test: tools/smoke/test_window_size.sh.

